  "review_scope": [
    "Default feature hooks are no-ops; profiling and transport remain host-selected and absent from project/gameplay mutation APIs.",
    "One process capture, mutex-protected fixed 25-phase/64-source aggregates, generation-fenced scope retirement, per-thread CPU ownership, nested inclusive timing, numeric identity bounds and failure/unwind handling.",
    "CountingAllocator forwards exact pointer/layout/size/null semantics without retaining pointers, locks or reentrant callbacks; failed realloc leaves original allocation/accounting intact; process requested-byte counters and nontransactional observation limits are explicit.",
    "QuickJS heap metrics occur after JS loans/budget checks and remain separate from Rust requested allocation counters. Actual runtime/script/game/player instrumentation preserves existing mutation and error order.",
    "Explicit player feature admission prevents transitive summary/Tracy feature unification from accepting a CLI option without its corresponding player report/transport feature.",
    "Pinned Tracy client manual startup has no implicit transport in a default build; process-owned standalone lifetime, fixed labels, numeric source slots, no unsafe shutdown. Upstream build flags and environment override surface reviewed.",
    "Observable tests cover stale scopes/workers, nested/failure cleanup, source quotas, same-allocator allocation/reallocation/null/zero/grow/shrink semantics, actual ScriptHost rollback/heap identity and player report/PCM parity."
  ],
